From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] avifil32: AVIFileExit undoes AVIFileInit

AVIFileInit initialises OLE on the calling thread; AVIFileExit, which lets go of the library, did nothing, so the thread stayed in its single-threaded apartment for good. It uninitialises OLE once per call now.
---
--- a/dlls/avifil32/api.c
+++ b/dlls/avifil32/api.c
@@ -180,9 +180,12 @@
  *		AVIFileExit		(AVIFIL32.@)
  */
 void WINAPI AVIFileExit(void) {
-  /* need to free ole32.dll if we are the last exit call */
-  /* OleUninitialize() */
-  FIXME("(): stub!\n");
+  /* (wine-sg 8263) the library's reference taken by AVIFileInit is let go: AVIFileInit initialised OLE on
+   * this thread, so each exit uninitialises it once */
+  TRACE("()\n");
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_AVIFILE_EXIT
+  OleUninitialize();
+#endif
 }
 
 /***********************************************************************
